A deployment's erasure process has a step for proxy usage data; it cannot complete until Skeid offers a way to delete (or anonymise) all usage rows of one organisation/API-key set. Needed: an admin call or CLI with a dry-run count, idempotent, and a result the platform can record.
Requested by a downstream deployment. Small commits per step.

2026-11-07 08:54 Also needed: a retention period for the usage tables Skeid writes (usage_events, usage_billed): how long rows are kept and a purge run, so a deployment's retention register can point to it.

